152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294157 13194139534548 true] [17592186294152 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534548 true] [17592186294152 1041 "selection" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294152 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294153 13194139534548 true] [17592186294152 1110 #uuid "ce80dd09-e6c0-5026-9933-9f24da3b1ce2" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294153 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2)" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294153 1111 #uuid "745f08d9-1eb8-52e3-94b1-fe8dac4c7444" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294154 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,3)" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294154 1111 #uuid "15335c6c-9de1-512f-8e37-6eea1794a3a5" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294155 1034 "x\\in (-3,2)" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294155 1111 #uuid "d33df2e9-e341-5866-82c4-64fea63b80a9" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294156 1034 "x\\in (0,2)" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294156 1111 #uuid "ea9afecf-6a07-5501-bd32-35059b4a6903" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294157 1034 "x\\in (-3,0)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294157 1111 #uuid "a3eda5c5-1086-500b-bb15-b55d2b8c5134" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294158 1017 #edb/ref 17592186294159 13194139534548 true] [17592186294158 1089 "q-116439" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294158 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534548 true] [17592186294158 1100 "Given $P(x)={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294158 1113 #uuid "88ba9665-3920-5271-b647-ee91ba660327" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294158 1145 "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+2x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+4x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x-2)+4(x-2)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+4)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}$ are $x=-4,$ $x=0$ and $x=2,$  where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-4$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/a357caad0365f296f87367ee4ac1000f1ea772d0d27650c8340d475ca742828b.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294160 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294161 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294162 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294163 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294164 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1041 "selection" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294160 13194139534548 true] [17592186294159 1110 #uuid "d9353a00-cc9b-570e-b83b-36de6f4e0e6e" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294160 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294160 1111 #uuid "399af956-c54f-5f1e-86b1-64b649a03fe7" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294161 1034 "x\\in (-4,2)" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294161 1111 #uuid "c3b1efc4-4d5b-5699-bda0-1f4193c4524c" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294162 1034 "x\\in (-4,0)\\cup (0,2)" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294162 1111 #uuid "05747928-0