-axis.\n\nFirst, we factorize the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-x-2) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+x-2x-2) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x+1)-2(x+1)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}$ are $x=-1,$ $x=0$ and $x=2,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-1$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/c0756761d00b0805683e447d8cee3b657bbbe004a0a47da428927585037b06c2.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294174 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294175 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294176 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294177 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186294178 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1041 "selection" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1104 #edb/ref 17592186294174 13194139534548 true] [17592186294173 1110 #uuid "1f189ece-3137-5595-951a-316be6645793" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294174 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty )" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294174 1111 #uuid "1c4073e8-f2fa-508a-9e58-9ac55da4fef3" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294175 1034 "x\\in (-1,2)" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534548 true] [17592186294175 1111 #uuid "c796b0ea-a4f0-55c1-b581-253020801a7b" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294176 1034 "x\\in (2,\\infty )" 13194139534548 true] [17592186294176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045